    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/25645?c=arizona": {
      "title": "On-Call Instructor (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "On-Call Instructor (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) On-Call Instructor (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions) Tucson, AZ, United States | req25645 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search On-Call Instructor (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions) Posting Number req25645 Department School of Health Professions Department Website Link https://healthprofessions.publichealth.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The DPT program is seeking local clinicians to participate in the program as associated on-call instructors.  Individuals hired for this position will act as instructors in their areas of expertise or lab assistants to support the core faculty. The position is PRN and hours and days worked will vary. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Teach content in the curriculum and/or assist core faculty during lab experiences. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold an active unrestricted PT license in Arizona or the equivalent for their profession if they are not Physical Therapists. Preferred Qualifications Experienced health care professional who is willing to share their expertise with DPT students. Clinical specialization and prior teaching experience is preferred. Rank Instructor Tenure Information Part-Time Hourly (NTE) FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week Varies Job FTE 0.025 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type hourly rate Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 26 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Dr. Christine Childers | cchilders@arizona.edu Open Date 4/8/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) and Cover Letter Special Instructions to Applicant Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27144?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Finance",
      "description": "Lecturer, Finance | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lecturer, Finance Tucson, AZ, United States | req27144 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/23/2026 Back to Search Lecturer, Finance Posting Number req27144 Department Finance Department Website Link https://eller.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The Department of Finance at the University of Arizona’s Eller College of Management is seeking applicants for a full-time Lecturer. Starting in the Spring 2027 semester, this position is expected to teach Finance courses and engage in student experience enrichment. This position will also have significant service responsibilities leading the Wall Street Scholars program, connecting department faculty with industry partners, and contributing to the academic strategy and operations of the department. The Department of Finance is one of seven academic units in the Eller College of Management offering undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs. It is internationally recognized for pioneering research, innovative curriculum, and distinguished faculty. Our mission is to discover and share new knowledge that shapes the future of business and to educate the next generation of responsible, global leaders who embody the changing business world and possess the knowledge and drive to impact it. We invite all qualified individuals to apply to join us in achieving our mission. This position is expected to teach primarily in person in Tucson. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; sick leave and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Finance. Lead the Wall Street Scholars program and connect department faculty and students with industry partners Contribute to the academic strategy and operations of the department. Other service activities may be assigned. Mentor students\nand/or student teams. Minimum Qualifications Master's\n     degree in Finance, Business Administration, or a related field. Teaching\n     experience at the college or university level, including at least one year\n     of in-person teaching experience. Experience\n     teaching to various audiences, evidenced by evaluations and/or awards. Must be available to\nteach in person at the University of Arizona in Tucson Arizona. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Finance, or related field, prior to the start date, OR 5 or more years of professional experience in finance, or equivalent. Experience developing and teaching college classes. Experience leading a student engagement program in an academic department or college. Rank Lecturer Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay $95,000-120,000 DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 1/4/2027 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Alice Bonaime, Department Head, alicebonaime@arizona.edu Open Date 9/16/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Three Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant Documents required to be submitted are: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) List of courses taught or assisted with, including your role/responsibilities associated with the courses Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Contact information for three references Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27067?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27067 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/23/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) Posting Number req27067 Department Speech Language & Hearing Sci Department Website Link https://slhs.arizona.edu Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The University of Arizona’s Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences seeks two full-time Speech-Language Pathology Clinical Faculty members to provide clinical services and participate in clinical education through supervising students at an otolaryngology clinic and the University clinic. One position will start around January 2027, and the other will start in July 2027. The Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences is renowned for its clinical training programs in Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology, as well as its active doctoral program. Our department includes 30 faculty members, 104 graduate students in three degree programs (M.S., Au.D, and Ph.D.), and 208 undergraduate students. Faculty in the department benefit from a rich collaborative environment within the University and the Southern Arizona communities. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This career-track appointment is not eligible for tenure. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Provide\n     clinical and instrumental assessment and treatment to patients with\n     communication, swallowing, or voice disorders\n     secondary to head and\n     neck cancer and progressive neurological diseases. Provide\n     clinical services at an otolaryngology clinic and the University clinic. Participate\n     in clinical education through supervising students in the context of their\n     caseload. Collaborate\n     with departmental faculty to provide evidence-based services. Assist\n     clinical program leadership with clinical administration or development as\n     assigned. Teach\n     in the classroom related to area/s of expertise as assigned. Clinical\n     program development. Ongoing\n     clinical and process improvement. Other\n     duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications, corresponding to rank: Master’s\n     or doctoral degree in      Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences, or equivalent. Three years of clinical\n     experience as a Speech-Language Pathologist working with patients with\n     voice or swallowing, and head and neck cancer, including TEP. License/license-eligibility\n     for practice in Speech-Language Pathology in the state of Arizona. Certificate\n     of Clinical Competence (CCC) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing\n     Association. Experience\n     with the adult patient      populations evaluated and treated in otolaryngology clinics. Preferred Qualifications More than five years of clinical experience. Experience with program development. Experience providing services to a variety of demographic populations. Experience with motor speech disorders. Experience with supervision. Spoken/written Spanish language skills. Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay $75,000 - $120,000 (depending on rank) Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 2 Target Hire Date 1/4/2027 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Robin Samlan, PhD, MBA, CCC-SLP Associate Professor, Associate Department Head & Director of Clinical Education rsamlan@arizona.edu Open Date 9/23/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants should attach the following materials: A cover letter that includes a description of your experience with and approach to clinical instruction. Your curriculum vitae (CV). Contact information for three professional references. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27083?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, Marketing (Career-Track) (Updated)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer, Marketing (Career-Track) (Updated) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Lecturer, Marketing (Career-Track) (Updated) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27083 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2026 Back to Search Senior Lecturer, Marketing (Career-Track) (Updated) Posting Number req27083 Department Marketing Department Website Link https://eller.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights Note: The work calendar for this position has been updated to Academic. The Department of Marketing at the University of Arizona’s Eller College of Management is seeking applicants for a full-time Senior Lecturer. Starting in the Fall 2027 semester, this position is expected to teach Marketing courses and engage in student experience enrichment. Initial course areas will require expertise in topics related to marketing strategy, including statistics and market research for decision making. This position is also expected to contribute to service leadership in the department. The Department of Marketing is one of seven academic units in the Eller College of Management offering undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs. It is internationally recognized for pioneering research, innovative curriculum, and distinguished faculty. Our mission is to discover and share new knowledge that shapes the future of business and to educate the next generation of responsible, global leaders who embody the changing business world and possess the knowledge and drive to impact it. We invite all qualified individuals to apply to join us in achieving our mission. This position is expected to teach primarily in person in Tucson. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Marketing. Participate in service responsibilities in the department, college, and/or university. Mentor students and/or student teams. Additional duties may\nbe assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's\n     degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a related field with\n     professional experience in topics related to marketing strategy, - OR - PhD in Marketing, or a related\nfield, prior to the start date. At\n     least six years of teaching experience at the college or university level,\n     including at least one year of in-person teaching experience. Experience\n     teaching multiple audiences, evidenced by evaluations and/or awards. Must be available to\nteach in person at the University of Arizona in Tucson Arizona. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing and teaching college classes. Experience in service leadership in an academic department, such as program director or academic area leader. Rank Senior Lecturer Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay $109,000 - $125,000, DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 8/16/2027 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Jesper Nielsen | jesper@arizona.edu Open Date 9/18/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Three Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant Documents required to be submitted are: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) Summary of courses taught and statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as summarized student evaluations and/or peer evaluations Contact information for three references Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27051?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice, Educational Leadership & Policy (CT) (COE) (Updated)",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice, Educational Leadership & Policy (CT) (COE) (Updated) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice, Educational Leadership & Policy (CT) (COE) (Updated) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27051 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice, Educational Leadership & Policy (CT) (COE) (Updated) Posting Number req27051 Department Educatnl Policy Studies Pract Department Website Link https://www.coe.arizona.edu/epsp Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights Please note that the job title for this position has been updated. This posting has been updated to reflect the date for reviewing applications. The Educational Leadership and Policy Unit in the Department of Educational Policy Studies and Practice is pleased to announce an opportunity to join our faculty. We are seeking candidates for the Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice (Career-Track), depending on qualifications and experience. We seek a collaborative colleague with leadership experience in PK–12 schools and/or districts who is ready to teach, mentor, and advise graduate students in online and in-person spaces. The candidate will join a highly varied and synergistic intellectual unit with an intentional focus on equity, anti-racism, social justice, and inclusion as these relate to education leadership and policy. The Search Committee will begin reviewing applications on November 2, 2026 and the position will begin in August 2027. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This career-track appointment is not eligible for tenure. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; sick leave and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Experience as an educational leader in PK-12 settings. Demonstrate experience and capacity to engage in leadership practice that is responsive to varied educational contexts and grounded in social justice theory and research. Responsibilities include designing and teaching graduate-level courses, both in-person and online, synchronously and  asynchronously, focused on educational leadership based on current theory and practice. The candidate must be prepared to engage in teaching, mentoring, and advising graduate students using asset-based approaches that affirm the: strengths and lived experiences of varied communities and the value of professional knowledge, while centering transformational change and leadership Relatedly, the candidate must demonstrate a willingness to advise master’s and doctoral students through programs of study, as well as through the design, development, and execution of capstone and dissertation research. Occasionally, this individual will represent the University at meetings and in partnerships with local and statewide districts, as well as with state and national organizations, to present relevant students, program, and department information and outcomes. Minimum Qualifications Earned Ph.D. or Ed.D. in education. Experience teaching courses in\nperson and online, synchronous and asynchronously. Proven accomplishment in\ndesigning pedagogy and curriculum to meet the needs of adult learners. Evidence of engaging in transformative leadership practice grounded in\nscholarship and varied PK-12 contexts. Demonstrated capacity for implementing\nasset-based approaches through supervision, advising, mentoring, coaching, or\nother professional growth opportunities. Demonstrated ability to represent the\nUniversity and build collaborative relationships/partnerships with local and\nstate-wide districts, and state and national organizations. Preferred Qualifications Principal experience in PK-12 schools. Possess a valid Arizona state administration certification or open to seeking a certification in Arizona. Expertise and experience in cross-disciplinary educational concepts. Experience teaching master’s and doctoral courses, in synchronous/asynchronous, online, hybrid, and/or face-to-face formats. Experience with academic writing and/or supporting students in developing academic writing skills. Experience chairing and/or serving on dissertation committees. Capacity to support in-person instruction, student mentoring, and partnerships with local school districts and/or state, national organizations; candidates located in or willing to establish residence in Tucson or the broader Arizona region are preferred. Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Cynthia Mruczek cmruczek@arizona.edu Open Date 9/16/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant For your application to be considered complete, please submit the following three documents: Curriculum Vitae – Current and complete. Cover Letter – Outlining your qualifications for this position. References - In the first additional document slot, provide the names and contact information, including phone numbers and email addresses, for THREE references. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27050?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Career Track Faculty, BSN (Tucson) (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Career Track Faculty, BSN (Tucson) (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Career Track Faculty, BSN (Tucson) (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27050 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Career Track Faculty, BSN (Tucson) (Part-Time) (Multiple Positions) Posting Number req27050 Department College of Nursing Department Website Link https://nursing.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights Join our nationally ranked, CCNE-accredited pre-licensure nursing program as a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Principal Lecturer OR Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor (FT) and help shape the future of nursing education. We're seeking passionate nurses for our traditional BSN program who are committed to innovative teaching and interdisciplinary collaboration. Make a meaningful impact in nursing education—apply today and become part of a supportive, dynamic academic environment driving excellence in healthcare. This career-track appointment is not eligible for tenure. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Teaching: Teach and guide students in theoretical and clinical practice courses within assigned program. Mentor students to support their academic success and professional growth. Create and maintain a positive, nursing values–driven learning environment. Evaluate student performance and contribute to ongoing curriculum development. Engage in program planning and assessment through faculty governance and continuous quality improvement. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and clinical partners to strengthen academic-practice relationships. Ensure compliance with program, college, and clinical site policies. Scholarship: Maintain clinical proficiency through direct or indirect practice. Develop academic excellence through practice-relevant inquiry and knowledge dissemination via publications and presentations. Contribute to grant efforts supporting student education and training. Service: Engage with faculty, the administrative leadership team, and students in furthering the mission and goals of the College of Nursing. Participate in special projects and faculty governance activities, as needed. There may be additional duties assigned as they relate to this position. Minimum Qualifications Rank to be determined by the college’s Faculty Appointment Promotion & Tenure (FAPT) Committee. All ranks: Graduate degree in nursing or a related field (must have a BSN, if graduate degree is non-nursing). Two (2) years of clinical experience as RN providing direct patient care. Evidence of teaching and clinical practice or systems leadership experience, through certification, or equivalent preparation. Provide evidence/receipt of an active Arizona RN License prior to first day of employment with College of Nursing. Maintain own license, immunizations, CPR, and other agency or College requirements and provide evidence of current status. Must be eligible to obtain a Level 1 Fingerprint Clearance Card from AZDPS. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, or DNP) in nursing or a related field (required for professorial track). Experience teaching nursing fundamentals, health assessment, or pediatric nursing in entry-to-practice nursing programs. Recent direct or indirect nursing practice. Experience in nursing simulation and student instruction. Experience in curriculum design, program evaluation, and active learning methods. Proficient in curriculum design, program evaluation, and active learning methods. Certified by a nationally recognized credentialing agency. Experience with online teaching methodologies. Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 20 Job FTE 0.5 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 2 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Lauren Acosta | heller@arizona.edu Open Date 9/16/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Three Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit all requested documents and complete the application in its entirety. In your Cover Letter, please address your teaching interest and/or experience with nursing fundamentals, health assessment, or pediatric nursing. \nCandidates are encouraged to review the College of Nursing appointment criteria for the Career-Track Lecturer Series and Career-Track Professorial Series. Applicants who wish to be considered for appointment at a specific or advanced rank should ensure that their CV and Cover Letter clearly demonstrate evidence consistent with the applicable rank criteria. Appointment series and rank will be determined based on the College of Nursing criteria for appointment to the Career-Track Lecturer or Career-Track Professorial series. Documents needed to apply: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Unofficial Academic Transcripts Proof of Current RN Licensure Names and Phone Numbers of at Least Three (3) Professional References Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26878?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Vice Chair, Research, Department of  Urology (MD) (College of Medicine - Phoenix)",
      "description": "Vice Chair, Research, Department of  Urology (MD) (College of Medicine - Phoenix) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Vice Chair, Research, Department of  Urology (MD) (College of Medicine - Phoenix) Phoenix, AZ, United States | req26878 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search Vice Chair, Research, Department of  Urology (MD) (College of Medicine - Phoenix) Posting Number req26878 Department COM Phx Urology Department Website Link College of Medicine-Phoenix Medical Sub-Speciality Urology Location Greater Phoenix Area Address 475 N. 5th Street, Phoenix, AZ 85004 USA Position Highlights The University of Arizona College of Medicine – Phoenix is seeking a vice chair of research in the Department of Urology. This is an opportunity for an outstanding leader with a national/international reputation as a respected and accomplished academician, clinician, educator and collaborator with a proven track record in innovating research. This position reports directly to the chair of the Department of Urology within the College of Medicine – Phoenix for all academic activities. Consistent with the Academic Affiliation Agreement (AAA) between the University of Arizona and Banner Health, the vice chair will have a matrix reporting relationship to the CEO of Banner – University Medical Group (B—UMG) and CEO of Banner – University Medical Center Phoenix (B—UMCP) for all clinical activities conducted at B—UMCP. The vice chair will assist the department in developing a research vision and infrastructure, seeking grant and other funding opportunities, serving as a principal investigator, developing research plans and methods, implanting and managing research studies and disseminating research findings. In addition, this individual will be expected to develop collaborative relationships with other university, college, clinical and community partners. The successful candidate will fulfill the responsibilities of a faculty member in the Department of Urology, actively participate in teaching, clinical service and/or scholarly work, and must qualify for an appointment at the rank of associate or full professor. The successful candidate will meet the requirements of a career track faculty according to the College and University guidelines. The University of Arizona College of Medicine – Phoenix anchors the 28-acre Phoenix Bioscience Core (PBC) in the heart of the Valley of the Sun. The College inspires and trains individuals to become exemplary physicians, scientists and leaders who are life-long learners and inquisitive scholars. The PBC campus embodies the University’s priorities of engagement, partnership, innovation, and synergy in its world-class academic and research initiatives, with clinical facilities throughout Greater Phoenix. Visa sponsorship is not available for this positions. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Develop and implement departmental research vision and infrastructure focusing on clinical trials, grantsmanship and original research. Build internal and external relationships to inspire and promote academic collaborations across the health system. Promote and provide a research and teaching environment of the highest quality and integrity. Foster programs of national distinction through innovation and collaboration. Mentor medical students, residents, fellows and faculty. Engage in teaching and research activities for students, residents and fellows. Participate on appropriate department and/or College committees as well as professional organizations, as appropriate. Minimum Qualifications Must\n     possess an MD or equivalent degree from an accredited instruction. Be\n     eligible for a University of Arizona academic appointment at the associate\n     professor level or higher. Be\n     board certified in Urology and be eligible for unrestricted medical\n     licensure in the State of Arizona. Be\n     eligible for medical staff membership at Banner – University Phoenix. Foster clinical and research programs of national distinction through innovation and interdisciplinary collaboration. Preferred Qualifications Have experience and national/international recognition in clinical trials. Demonstrate experience with hospital partnership and collaboration. Have developed a research portfolio including NIH or industry grants. Be experienced as a PI. Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay AAMC Public Schools for Rank and Specialty Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Office of Human Resources, Talent Acquisition talent@arizona.edu Open Date 8/25/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Application: The online application should be completed in its entirety. Blank or missed information may be considered an incomplete submission. CV and cover letter required for to be considered for the position. One additional document will be professional reference contacts. Please include at least three professional references at your current rank or above, their contact information and the nature of your work with them. Faculty selected for this teaching opportunity will be required to obtain faculty status within the appropriate academic department. This will include obtaining letters of recommendation and review by the appropriate College review committee. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
