    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26750?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Limited Term Adjunct for DNP Program (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Limited Term Adjunct for DNP Program (Multiple Positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Limited Term Adjunct for DNP Program (Multiple Positions) Tucson, AZ, United States | req26750 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/10/2026 Back to Search Limited Term Adjunct for DNP Program (Multiple Positions) Posting Number req26750 Department College of Nursing Department Website Link https://nursing.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address 1305 N Martin Ave, Tucson, AZ 85721 USA Position Highlights Are you ready to be part of something extraordinary? The University of Arizona, College of Nursing is actively seeking talented limited term adjunct instructors for our cutting-edge graduate programs, including our dynamic online offerings. As an instructor, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the future of nursing education. Reporting to the Instructor on Record, you will have the opportunity to collaborate closely with the program coordinator and Lead Faculty, working hand-in-hand to deliver exceptional instruction and provide valuable mentorship to our students. With a commitment to excellence, we strive to create an engaging and inclusive learning environment that prepares our students for success. Located in the breathtaking valley, surrounded by majestic mountains, our Tucson campus at the University of Arizona offers not only a stunning natural landscape but also a rich cultural diversity that enriches our educational experience. As one of the nation's most esteemed research institutions, the University of Arizona is at the forefront of health-sciences education and scholarship, offering an environment that fosters innovation and encourages groundbreaking discoveries. We take immense pride in our College of Nursing, accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education, which consistently ranks among the top 15 percent of graduate nursing programs in the United States. By joining our esteemed faculty, you become part of a community dedicated to pushing boundaries and advancing the field of nursing. If you are passionate about nursing education, excited to embrace innovation, and ready to make a lasting impact, this is the opportunity you've been waiting for. Join us in shaping the future of healthcare through education and become part of our exceptional team at the College of Nursing. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Collaborate with the Program Director and other Program Lead Faculty to teach and guide students. Facilitate course learning activities, including testing and evaluation. Participate in course evaluation and continuous course improvement. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing or other health-related field. Active certification as a nurse practitioner. Experience in mentoring or teaching health care professionals. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Nursing or other health-related field. Successful college or university teaching experience. Experience with a variety of teaching methods and curricular perspectives. Experience in online learning and course development. Rank Instructor Tenure Information Adjunct (NTE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week TBD Job FTE 0.1-0.4 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 5 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Lindsay Bouchard | labouchard@arizona.edu Open Date 8/10/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) and Cover Letter Special Instructions to Applicant Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26726?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, TFTV (Multiple Positions)(UPDATED)",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, TFTV (Multiple Positions)(UPDATED) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Instructor, TFTV (Multiple Positions)(UPDATED) Tucson, AZ, United States | req26726 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/6/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Instructor, TFTV (Multiple Positions)(UPDATED) Posting Number req26726 Department Sch Theatre Film & Television Department Website Link https://tftv.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights Note: Two additional positions have been added to this recruitment. The University of Arizona, School of Theatre, Film & Television is accepting applications for Adjunct Instructors to teach Arts Administration courses during the 2026-2027 Academic Year. Appointments may be assigned as semester or academic year long. This is a unique opportunity to work with undergraduate and graduate students. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the\nUniversity of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Instruct\n     in field of assigned expertise Hold\n     regular office hours. Assign\n     grades to students, based upon performance in class assignments and\n     exams/juries. Attend\n     meetings as required. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's\n     degree in relevant field or equivalent professional experience,\n     credentials or certification. Minimum of 2 years teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications Terminal Degree in related discipline. 4 years University level teaching experience in related discipline. Rank Instructor Tenure Information Adjunct (NTE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 8 - 19 Job FTE .20 - .49 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay $45,000 Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 3 Target Hire Date 8/24/2026 Expected End Date 1/3/2027 Contact Information for Candidates Frances Gateward, TFTV Director, gateward@arizona.edu Open Date 8/6/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Resume, Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Documents required to apply: Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and a document containing contact information for 3 references. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26673?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Simulation Nurse (On-Call) (Part-Time) (Gilbert, AZ)",
      "description": "Simulation Nurse (On-Call) (Part-Time) (Gilbert, AZ) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Simulation Nurse (On-Call) (Part-Time) (Gilbert, AZ) Gilbert, AZ, United States | req26673 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/31/2026 Back to Search Simulation Nurse (On-Call) (Part-Time) (Gilbert, AZ) Posting Number req26673 Department College of Nursing Department Website Link https://nursing.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Greater Phoenix Area Address 92 W. Vaughn Ave, Suite 301, Gilbert, AZ 85233 USA Position Highlights The College of Nursing Simulation Nurse is responsible for supporting a healthcare simulation laboratory learning environment based on contemporary best practices, leading edge technology and the testing of new approaches. The Simulation Nurse will collaborate with the U of A College of Nursing Simulation team and under the direction of the Director and Site Coordinator work with faculty to support student skills acquisition, deliberative practice, and simulation-based education activities. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please Duties & Responsibilities Simulation and skills related: Prepare   and maintain clinical laboratory and simulation environments with extreme   attention to detail including props and moulage. Set-up,   reset and take-down simulation, deliberative practice, remediation, and   testing environments. Support   faculty and staff during planning, trialing, validation, and running of   laboratory and/or simulation-based education activities. Assist   students and faculty with use of technology (simulators, computers, and   audio-visual equipment). Operate   simulators according to scenario guides and activity specifications. Perform   manikin software programing and implement simulated scenarios. Demonstrate   application of simulation-based education best practices. Contribute   to development and refinement of simulation-based activities. Provide   remediation support to students according to faculty specifications and   communicate student’s progress per CON policies. Inventory and maintenance related: Participate   in efficient and cost-effective management of consumable supplies, durable   resources, and manikin maintenance including minor repairs, preventative maintenance,   and general cleanliness. Assist   in maintaining organized ongoing supply inventory, placing orders, and   stocking supplies. Maintain   inventory, par stock and related documents for consumable and durable   laboratory resources. Maintain   testing supplies separate from lab kits and open stock to ensure needed items   are on-hand for testing. Restock,   organize, and maintain supply areas and carts. Provide   ongoing support and management of student laboratory kits. Other: Maintain   awareness and careful use of simulation-based education activities   calendar(s). Participate   in CON simulation team meetings and assigned work groups. Support   development and refinement of processes, policies, and procedures. Utilize   software, applications, and databases as directed. Support   orientation and mentoring of new faculty and staff. Work   with volunteer students as assigned. Assist   with tours and events for a variety of groups and organizations. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of 3 years of relevant work experience is required. Bachelor's degree in Nursing. RN licensure and graduation from an accredited nursing\nprogram required. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) and/or Certified Healthcare Simulation Operations Specialists (CHSOS). Experience with a variety of high-fidelity manikins and software. Simulation-based education experience. Interprofessional education experience. Integrative Health related experience. Doctoral degree in Nursing, Education or Healthcare. Rank Instructor Tenure Information FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week Varies Job FTE 0.025 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay $40.00 - $50.00 Compensation Type hourly rate Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 3 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Dr. Janine Hinton | hintonje@arizona.edu Open Date 7/31/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) and Cover Letter Special Instructions to Applicant Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26632?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Senior Capstone, Civil and Architectural Engineering and Mechanics",
      "description": "Adjunct Lecturer, Senior Capstone, Civil and Architectural Engineering and Mechanics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Lecturer, Senior Capstone, Civil and Architectural Engineering and Mechanics Tucson, AZ, United States | req26632 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/27/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Lecturer, Senior Capstone, Civil and Architectural Engineering and Mechanics Posting Number req26632 Department Civil Arch Engr and Mechanics Department Website Link caem.engineering.arizona.edu Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The Department of Civil and Architectural Engineering and Mechanics invites qualified applicants to apply for an Adjunct Lecturer position. Our current need is for an Adjunct Lecturer to teach our senior capstone design sequence that includes courses CE 408A, Issues Civil Engr Practice, and CE 408B, CE Senior Capstone Design, in the fall and spring of academic year 2026-27, respectively. This is anticipated to be a 0.0625 - 0.25 FTE position (Full Academic Year). CE 408A is an introduction to non-technical issues impacting the practice of design professionals in the private and public sectors including:  types of organizations, income, expenses, and profit; quality-based selection for obtaining and performing work; contracts; dispute resolution methods; professional ethics.  The instructor, or invited practitioner experts, will present lectures on the topics.  The design project is introduced in the Fall semester and the major students products are a Statement of Qualifications and a Design Concept Report (DCR).  The instructor will act as project manager, form project teams, and meet regularly with teams to monitor progress and address issues/concerns. CE 408B focuses on the design with technical lectures to support student efforts.  Technical lectures may be provided by faculty or practitioners.  In addition to responding to comments on the DCR, students will submit required intermediate design review(s) and a final presentation.  The instructor will regularly meet with students on progress and address issues/concerns and organize the final review panels.  Industry practitioners can provide expertise and serve as secondary project managers. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the\nUniversity of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Three hours of lecture per\n       week (Tuesdays and Thursdays from 5:00pm to 6:15pm).  The course syllabus and material will\n       be provided by the department head. Lecture time may consist of classroom activities,\n       team/discipline meetings, project related meetings and/or other activities as necessary. Prepare and assign various assignments (e.g., homework,\n       quizzes, etc) to complement and assess team learning activities. Coordinate with grader that\n       will help grading assignments Communicate and collaborate\n       with other practitioner experts as needed. Be accessible by students\n       in office hours that may meet on campus or via phone/Zoom during their\n       instructional period. Also, the lecturer should be available via email\n       throughout the week. Enter grades into the UA\n       online system. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s\n     Degree Must\n     have a PE license Must demonstrate experience, a strong working\nknowledge and excellence in Civil Engineering business Preferred Qualifications A record of service to the profession, and a demonstrated ability to work effectively with practitioners is preferred. Experience teaching at the university level with preference to having taught this or a similar course. Rank Lecturer Tenure Information Adjunct (NTE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 5 – 10 Job FTE 0.0625 - 0.25 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay $5,500 - $11,000 Compensation Type Per Course Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 8/14/2026 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Dominic Boccelli, Department Head dboccelli@arizona.edu Open Date 7/27/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Application material: Cover Letter CV Candidates must describe their interest in the position and any relevant teaching experience in the teaching statement. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26555?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Limited Term Adjunct Instructor (Chinese) (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Limited Term Adjunct Instructor (Chinese) (Multiple Positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Limited Term Adjunct Instructor (Chinese) (Multiple Positions) Tucson, AZ, United States | req26555 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/23/2026 Back to Search Limited Term Adjunct Instructor (Chinese) (Multiple Positions) Posting Number req26555 Department Humanities Administration Department Website Link https://ltc.arizona.edu/ Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The University of Arizona Language Training Center (LTC) is currently hiring Instructors for short-term intensive Chinese language courses. Funded by the Defense Language and National Security Education Office, the LTC offers language instruction certification and advanced training in multiple strategic languages. Alumni Jacquelynn and Bennett Dorrance have made a gift commitment of $5.4 million to endow the deanship of the University of Arizona College of Humanities and inspire on campus and throughout the world a continuous and fearless spirit of open inquiry: Jacquelynn and Bennett Dorrance The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Prepare lesson plans and instruct sessions according to\n     approved curriculum. Attend pre-course meetings with Program\n     Manager/Executive Director. Understand Defense Language Proficiency Test (DLPT) and\n     Interagency Language Roundtable (ILR) score levels. Develop the course(s) curriculum and lesson plans with\n     authentic reading and listening materials. Build, update curriculum and course materials. Answer student emails and communicate regularly with\n     students. Provide communication and feedback to students\n     throughout the course. Submit lesson plans and course/teaching materials to\n     LTC Program Manager for teaching material archive. Communicate and/or meet with center directors, other\n     instructors in the same teaching team, and LTC staff as needed. Provide feedback to Program Manager/Executive Director\n     on course(s) as needed. Additional duties as required by supervisor. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in related field. Native or near-native fluency in the Chinese language. Prior experience in teaching language courses. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree in Chinese language pedagogy, second/foreign language education, applied linguistics, or other relevant field. Prior experience in curriculum development. Prior experience in teaching beginner through advanced intensive language courses and demonstrated excellence in teaching. Rank Instructor Tenure Information Adjunct (NTE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 9.6 - 19.6 hours/wk Job FTE .24 - .49 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay $3,000 - $13,500 Compensation Type Per Course Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 3 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates GT Russell gtrussell@arizona.edu Open Date 7/23/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) Special Instructions to Applicant Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
