    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26135?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Simulation Nurse (On-Call)",
      "description": "Simulation Nurse (On-Call) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Simulation Nurse (On-Call) Tucson, AZ, United States | req26135 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 5/29/2026 Back to Search Simulation Nurse (On-Call) Posting Number req26135 Department College of Nursing Department Website Link https://nursing.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address 1305 N Martin Ave, Tucson, AZ 85721 USA Position Highlights Join the University of Arizona College of Nursing and help shape the next generation of healthcare professionals through innovative, hands-on simulation-based education in a collaborative academic environment. The College of Nursing Simulation Nurse is responsible for supporting a healthcare simulation laboratory learning environment based on contemporary best practices, leading edge technology and the testing of new approaches. The Simulation Nurse will collaborate with the U of A College of Nursing Simulation team and, under the direction of the Director and Site Coordinator, work with faculty to support student skills acquisition, deliberative practice, and simulation-based education activities. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Simulation and skills\n  related: Prepare and maintain clinical laboratory and\n       simulation environments with extreme attention to detail including props\n       and moulage. Sets-up, reset and take-down simulation,\n       deliberative practice, remediation, and testing environments. Support faculty and staff during planning,\n       trialing, validation, and running of laboratory and/or simulation-based\n       education activities. Assist students and faculty with use of\n       technology (simulators, computers, and audio-visual equipment). Operate simulators according to scenario guides\n       and activity specifications. Perform manikin software programing and\n       implement simulated scenarios. Demonstrate application of simulation-based\n       education best practices. Contribute to development and refinement of\n       simulation-based activities. Provide remediation support to students\n       according to faculty specifications and communicate student’s progress\n       per CON policies. Inventory and maintenance\n  related: Participate in efficient and cost-effective\n       management of consumable supplies, durable resources, and manikin maintenance including minor repairs, preventative maintenance, and\n       general cleanliness. Assist in maintaining organized ongoing supply\n       inventory, placing orders, and stocking supplies. Maintain inventory, par stock and related\n       documents for consumable and durable laboratory resources. Maintain testing supplies separate from lab kits\n       and open stock to ensure needed items are on-hand for testing. Restock, organize, and maintain supply areas and\n       carts. Provide ongoing support and management of\n       student laboratory kits. Other: Maintain awareness and careful use of\n       simulation-based education activities calendar(s). Participate in CON simulation team meetings and\n       assigned work groups. Support development and refinement of processes,\n       policies, and procedures. Utilize software, applications, and databases as\n       directed. Support orientation and mentoring of new faculty\n       and staff. Work with volunteer students as assigned. Assist with tours and events for a variety of\n       groups and organizations. Minimum Qualifications A minimum of (3)\n     years of relevant work experience is required. Bachelor's\n     degree. RN\nlicensure and graduation from an accredited nursing program required. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Nursing, Education, or Healthcare. Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE). Certified Healthcare Simulation Operations Specialists (CHSOS). Experience with a variety of high-fidelity manikins and software. Simulation-based education experience. Interprofessional education experience. Integrative Health related experience. Tenure Information Part-Time Hourly (NTE) FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 1 Job FTE 0.025 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay $40.00 - $50.00 Compensation Type hourly rate Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 5 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Dr. Janine Hinton | hintonje@arizona.edu Open Date 5/29/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) and Cover Letter Special Instructions to Applicant Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/26089?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Lecturer, LIS/Data Science/Creative Computing (UPDATED)",
      "description": "Lecturer, LIS/Data Science/Creative Computing (UPDATED) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lecturer, LIS/Data Science/Creative Computing (UPDATED) United States | req26089 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 5/22/2026 Back to Search Lecturer, LIS/Data Science/Creative Computing (UPDATED) Posting Number req26089 Department Information Science Department Website Link https://infosci.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location To Be Determined Address USA Position Highlights Note: The\napplication window has been updated. The University of Arizona's College of Information Science invites you to apply to the role of Lecturer. The University of Arizona College of Information Science focuses on the intersection of people, data, and technology, offering innovative programs in information science, data science, cybersecurity, game design, and immersive technologies. Established in 2023 and expanded in 2025, the college provides STEM-designated undergraduate and master’s degrees, as well as a PhD in Information. With nationally ranked programs such as the #1 Best Online Bachelor’s in Cybersecurity, #4 Best Master’s in Data Science, and #10 Global Ranking of Library an Information Science Programs, the college emphasizes computational thinking, ethical reasoning, and multicultural communication while driving research and partnerships such as the Arizona Cybersecurity Academy, AI Core, Gaming and Virtual Worlds, Human-Centered Computing, and many other areas of research. The Lecturer for LIS/Data Science/Creative Computing will provide instruction in areas of advanced cyber operations and AI-focused cybersecurity. NOTE: FTE will be based on course availability, assignment may be classroom-based, virtual, or some combination thereof, depending on need and instructor preference. This career-track appointment is not eligible for tenure. Candidates working anywhere in the U.S. may be considered for a remote assignment. If you are selected for this position and are employed to work remotely from outside of Arizona, your overtime exemption status will depend on the laws of the state where you perform your work. For employees working outside of Arizona, you may be hired as an hourly employee in accordance with state laws, and your position title would be “Part-Time Faculty” instead of “Lecturer” in accordance with university practices. These changes would not affect the position duties as outlined. An hourly rate for this position would be $46.88 - $56.25 per hour. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; sick leave and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuitionreduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please visit talent.arizona.edu Duties & Responsibilities Instruct students in field of expertise. Plan course delivery, align content with other courses as needed, and provide feedback on student work. Advise students, hold office hours, and provide student support. Assist with Capstone projects or individual student projects as needed, engaging in project-based pedagogy when possible. Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree in Information Science, Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Engineering, Library Science, media Ecology, Gam Media, Gaming Behavior, Game Design and Production, Game Development, or other related field. Preferred Qualifications Content expertise that aligns with enrollment needs. Rank Lecturer Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 20-40 Job FTE .50-1.00 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay $75,000-$90,000 Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 8/17/2026 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates HR-infosci@arizona.edu Open Date 5/22/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) and Cover Letter Special Instructions to Applicant The application window is anticipated to close on Monday, August 31, 2026. . Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
