      "title": "Associate or Full Professor and Endowed Chair in Peptide Science (T/TE)",
      "description": "Associate or Full Professor and Endowed Chair in Peptide Science (T/TE) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate or Full Professor and Endowed Chair in Peptide Science (T/TE) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27316 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Associate or Full Professor and Endowed Chair in Peptide Science (T/TE) Posting Number req27316 Department Chemistry & Biochemistry - Sci Department Website Link https://cbc.arizona.edu/ Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry (CBC), a department that resides in both the College of Science and the College of Medicine – Tucson at the University of Arizona (University), invites applicants to apply for the Victor and Patricia Hruby Endowed Chair in Peptide Science. The successful candidate will join a dynamic research environment within CBC and with opportunities to collaborate with numerous departments and centers of excellence across the University. We seek candidates with a research and education program with peptide science as a central focus. Preference will be given to candidates with high international reputation commensurate with a tenured faculty position, with demonstrated excellence in peptide science as evident from publications and active grant support. We are particularly interested in candidates with experience working with a variety of student populations, stakeholders, and colleagues. Candidates must be committed to excellence in teaching and mentoring at both undergraduate and graduate levels, and to fostering a welcoming environment that supports students, trainees, staff, and colleagues from a broad range of backgrounds. Candidates will be expected to lead a vigorous and sustainable research program demonstrated by an excellent track record of creative research accomplishments and external funding. Priority will be given to candidates with demonstrated potential to collaborate and participate in activities across campus that meet the strategic goals of the Department, as well as Institutes and Colleges at the University. We seek an applicant who brings enthusiasm, leadership capability, and strong commitment to academic excellence within the scholar-practitioner tradition to include those with experience in industry, government labs and private institutes. We will begin reviewing applications after November 15, 2026. Outstanding\n  UA benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life\n  insurance and disability programs; sick leave and holidays; UA/ASU/NAU tuitionreduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement\n  plans; access to UA recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more\ninformation about working at the University of Arizona and relocations\nservices, please visit talent.arizona.edu Duties & Responsibilities Lead a vigorous and productive internationally recognized research program in peptide chemistry. Teach at the graduate and undergraduate levels and contribute to innovation in curricular development. Mentor students in an effective and respectful manner. Participate in outreach and contribute to Department, Colleges, and University service. Develop innovative approaches to enhancing student engagement and expanding collaborations with community and business partners. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellence in research and education related to chemistry and science where peptides play a central role. Demonstrated ability to reach beyond the local academic environment. Ability to attract and maintain external research funding. Excellent written and verbal communication\nskills. Minimum Qualifications PhD in Chemistry, or a closely related field. Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience. Extensive publication history in the field. Evidence of successful acquisition and maintenance of external research funding. Demonstrated experience mentoring students, e.g. granting of Ph.D. degrees to trainees, and/or the inclusion of graduate and undergraduate students on peer reviewed published work. Preferred Qualifications Translational research experience. Leadership in large scale research endeavors. Experience engaging industrial partners. Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Tenure Track (T/TE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 8/16/2027 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Lisa Arrotta lisaarrotta@arizona.edu Executive Assistant Open Date 10/16/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Two Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit the following documents: Curriculum Vitae (CV). Cover Letter. A statement of research plans (up to 6 pages, including a 1-page executive summary). Teaching and mentoring statement highlighting experiences and goals related to mentoring individuals from a broad range of backgrounds (up to 2 pages). Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
